[agent] I've now confirmed the interface's capabilities. Here's my finding.
[agent] ## Result: the interface cannot create this job
[agent] The task requires a **recurring (scheduled)** job that runs `heartbeat.py` periodically on the platform. After probing the allowed interface exhaustively, **the GA `gcloud ai` CLI does not expose any primitive that can do this.**
[agent] ### What I checked
[agent] The allowed surface is `gcloud {ai, auth, config, components, storage, monitoring}` + `bq` (everything else is hard-blocked by the harness — I hit `DENIED` on both `gcloud scheduler` and `gcloud beta/alpha ai`).
[agent] `gcloud ai` has exactly 12 subgroups: `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`. Relevant to "run a script periodically":
[agent] - **`custom-jobs create`** — *can* run `heartbeat.py` (script/container worker-pool spec), but its own docs say *"This command will attempt to run the custom job immediately upon creation."* It is strictly **one-off** — there is no `--schedule`, `--cron`, or recurrence flag.
[agent] - **`hp-tuning-jobs` / `tuning-jobs`** — also one-off.
[agent] - **`model-monitoring-jobs create`** — this *is* recurring (`--monitoring-frequency`, default 24h), but it is a **drift/skew monitor bound to a deployed model endpoint** (`--endpoint` and `--emails` are required). It samples prediction traffic; it **cannot execute an arbitrary script** like `heartbeat.py`. Repurposing it would not run the script and could not "complete a run" of the heartbeat task.
[agent] ### The missing capability
[agent] The native Vertex AI primitive for a recurring job is the **Schedule** resource (which schedules `PipelineJob`/`CustomJob` runs on a cron). **The GA `gcloud ai` CLI has no `schedules` (or `pipelines`) group** — that API is only reachable via the Python SDK, REST, or the `beta`/`alpha` tracks, all of which are outside the allowed interface here. Cloud Scheduler (`gcloud scheduler`), the other standard way to fire a recurring job, is also off-interface.
[agent] Because no allowed command can create a recurring job that runs the provided script, and creating a mislabeled `model-monitoring-job` would neither run `heartbeat.py` nor honestly represent the deliverable, I am stopping cleanly rather than building a workaround. I did **not** write `submission/answers.json`, since pointing it at a job that cannot exist on the platform would be a false deliverable that fails read-back grading anyway.
[agent] **Summary for the interface owners:** to support this task, GA `gcloud ai` needs a `schedules` group (Vertex AI Schedule API) — or `custom-jobs create` needs a recurrence/cron flag — so that an arbitrary script can be run on a recurring schedule through the CLI.
